From 0561b39392ef9178a51eb72820d701a8303a41c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sijie52 <sijie5452@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:07:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(c): add tree-sitter C parser for YASA UAST

Start from the earlier parser-c prototype and make it produce a correct
UAST for real C code:

- emit one VariableDeclaration per declarator (the prototype compared
  web-tree-sitter wrappers by reference and added a phantom `_` per
  declaration) and read declarators inside-out
- keep every #if/#ifdef/#else branch instead of dropping them, so header
  guards no longer hide whole files
- expand object-like and function-like macros defined in the file,
  preferring portable definitions over _WIN32-only ones
- parse hex/octal/binary/suffixed numbers, decode string and char
  escapes, join adjacent strings, map typedefs, unions, designated and
  positional initializer lists
- allow assignment through `*p`, recover complete constructs inside
  tree-sitter ERROR regions, degrade unsupported statements to Noop and
  record syntax errors in CompileUnit._meta.parseErrors (strict mode
  throws)
- drop per-node source text from _meta, which made UAST size quadratic

Add 50 unit tests and a CI workflow mirroring the Python parser.
